The project in one line
Mangy = an emotion-conditioned ambient music engine (Rust, CPU-only, no GPU) + a scientific lab + a thesis. It generates ambient/techno/drone tracks from real chord data, predicts emotion, and tests its own hypotheses.
Repo
/home/box/Documents/patala (monorepo). Start with docs/README.md (index) and docs/HANDOVER_NEXT.md (continuation + vision).
Low-RAM rules (non-negotiable)
- cargo -j 2, ninja -j 1, detached builds (setsid nohup ... & disown), kill by PID (not pkill). 4 GB machine. Never load big files whole.
What works right now (tested, exposed via API)
- Engine (soundworld/src/): brainwave (binaural tone bed), seq (note sequencer + style patches + influence %), emotion (valence/arousal + fit), rasa (6D chord-graph + 9 rasas), neurosynth (focus arc), drone, corpus/producer (real-audio hybrid), eval/tune (closed-loop), live (realtime), harmony_data (seeded with real CHORDONOMICON priors).
- API: /commands (all mechanisms), /llm, /harmony, /verify, /evaluate, /state. MCP server (mcp/mangy_mcp.py) exposes it to any LLM agent.
- 62+ tests pass.
- Scientific lab (tools/study/run_study.py) runs H1–H3 on real CHORDONOMICON data → tools/study/STUDY_RESULTS.md. H1/H2 supported; H3 framed.
- Real data: data/chordonomicon/chord_transitions.json (from 4,556 songs); 3 CC-ambient refs.
